 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It depends on the couple. Some split it evenly, others take turns at the parents' houses, and some split it based on income. That's fair. Ask his parents if they have a preference, and if they say nothing, let it rest with your parents' offer. Not rude. It' just not common for couples to ask both sets. Then you and your partner cover it together, and maybe pay them back with a gift. That's the kindest thing. Show them the wedding invitation when you ask, just in case.",
